    "masking_description": "",
    "intervention_model_description": "Patients will be categorized into 4 groups: the first group will undergo 15 minutes intravenous infusion of furosemide combined with hypertonic saline solution (100 mL) twice daily along with severe water restriction (\\< 500 mL); the second group will receive intravenous furosemide as a bolus twice daily and severe water restriction (\\< 500 mL) without hypertonic saline solution; the third group will undergo 15 minutes intravenous infusion of furosemide combined with hypertonic saline solution (100 mL) twice daily, severe water restriction (\\< 500 mL), and SGLT2 inhibitors (Dapagliflozin); the fourth group will receive intravenous furosemide as a bolus without hypertonic saline solution twice daily, severe water restriction (\\< 500 mL), and SGLT2 inhibitors (Dapagliflozin).",
